Ground truth: 27
Response[0]:
<start_working_out>
To solve this problem, we can first find the total number of brown and white bears Gino has, and then subtract this total from the total number of bears he has.
15 (brown bears) + 24 (white bears) = 39
66 (total bears) - 39 (brown and white bears) = 27
So, Gino has 27 black bears.
<end_working_out>

